  "term": "2-AG",
  "definition": "2-AG is an endogenous molecule called 2-arachidonoylglycerol that is normally broken down by the enzyme MGLL. When its levels rise, it increases cannabinoid receptor signaling in the central nervous system, which helps modulate neurotransmission and can reduce overactive neural signaling.",
